INT. PRESCHOOL PLAYGROUND - NAP TIME - AFTERNOON

Foam mats. Mobile of felt moons. Six figures in miniature chairs at a very small table, holding very small teacups.

GRANDMA ODALIE KOWALSKI-ADEYEMI (70s, church hat). UNCLE BARTHOLOMEW "BERTIE" NNAMDI-LINDGREN (50s, delivery uniform). AUNT RUFINA PRYCE-OYELARAN (40s, scrubs). COUSIN TAVIAN BRAITHWAITE-OSEI (30s, suit). THE BABY SITTER, MS. JOSEPHINE "JOJO" ABARA-FENWICK (20s, lanyard). And the child, LITTLE ZURI ADEKUNLE-HOLM (4, tutu over snow pants).

ZURI
(solemn)
More tea, please.

ODALIE
Of course, dear.

She pours from an empty pot. Bertie sips from a cup of nothing. Rufina checks her watch. Tavian's phone buzzes; he silences it. Jojo mouths along with every word.

ZURI
She spilled.

BERTIE
She did?

RUFINA
She did not.

TAVIAN
She did a little.

ODALIE
He's lying. She spilled a lot.

ZURI
He did it.

JOJO
Who's he?

ZURI
Him.

Everybody points at somebody else.

ZURI (CONT'D)
Nap time!

They lower their heads onto the table, one by one, a perfect silent tableau. Zuri peeks. Smiles. Lowers her head too.
